title: Glossary
tags: Documentation
kind: reference
aliases: terms definitions
summary: Every term of metafolder in one line, with the note that defines it.

!! Data

* ''Metarecord'' — the unit of metadata: a uuid, a version and fields, about one subject — a file, a tag, a collection ([[Metarecord]]).
* ''Field'' — a name and a typed value on a metarecord; several fields may share a name, never the same value twice ([[Fields and values]], [[No duplicate rows]]).
* ''Value type'' — one of ten: `nothing`, `string`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `datetime`, `ref`, `tree_ref`, `ref_base`, `external_ref` ([[Value types]]); a field name has one in the whole repository ([[One value type per field name]]).
* ''Nothing'' — a value saying "this field does not apply"; ''unknown'' is the field not being there at all ([[Nothing versus unknown]]).
* ''Field spec'' — `name:type=value`, a field as written on the command line ([[Field specifications]]).
* ''Reference'' (`ref`) — a value pointing at another metarecord ([[Following references]]).
* ''TreeRef'' (`tree_ref`) — a value placing a metarecord under a parent, with a name; the ''position'' of that metarecord ([[TreeRef forest]], [[One position per forest]]).
* ''Forest'' — the trees one `tree_ref` field name draws; `mfr_path` is the forest of files ([[TreeRef forest]]).
* ''Path'' — a position read from its root down, `/`-separated, relative to the repository root ([[Path representation]], [[TreeRef path conventions]]).
* ''Reserved field'' — `mfr_*` is written by the daemon, `mf_*` is read by it ([[Reserved fields]]).
* ''Version'' — a hash of a metarecord's content, compared for equality only ([[Metarecord version]]).
* ''Schema'' — the declared types of metarecords and the constraints on their fields ([[Schema]]).

!! Repositories and the daemon

* ''Repository'' — a directory tree and its metadata store, in `.metafolder/` ([[Repository]], [[Repository layout on disk]]).
* ''Root metarecord'' — the metarecord of the repository's root directory, whose path is empty; it carries the tracking defaults ([[Watch and ignore fields]]).
* ''Store'' — the on-disk key-value database of one repository ([[Storage]]).
* ''Daemon'' — the background server holding the loaded repositories ([[Daemon]]).
* ''Loading'' — making the daemon work on a repository; one daemon at a time, enforced by a lock ([[Creating and loading a repository]], [[The repository lock]]).
* ''Session token'' — the secret every request to the daemon carries ([[Session tokens]]).
* ''Task'' — long daemon work that can be observed and often stopped ([[Tasks]]).
* ''Slow log'' — the record of the operations that took too long ([[Slow log]]).
* ''Configuration repository'' — `~/.config/metafolder/`, a git repository of every setting ([[Configuration]]).

!! Queries

* ''Query'' — a condition selecting metarecords ([[Query]]).
* ''DSL'' — the query language in its full, exact form ([[Writing queries]], [[Query DSL grammar]]).
* ''Simplified query'' — a shorter language, expanded into the DSL by an editable grammar ([[Simplified query language]]).
* ''Aspect'' — the part of a value a predicate reads: `field:value`, `field:parent`, `field:path` ([[Field aspects]]).
* ''osm'' — ordered substring matching, the finder-style match ([[Ordered substring matching]]).
* ''Selector'' — how a command names its metarecords: `-i`, `-q`, or none for all ([[Selectors]]).
* ''Cursor'' — the mark a paged query hands back to continue from ([[Pagination and sorting]]).

!! File tracking

* ''Tracked'' — having a metarecord with an `mfr_path`; ''watched'' — being followed live ([[File tracking]]).
* ''Eligible'' — inside a watched folder and not ignored ([[Eligibility]]).
* ''Watch'' and ''ignore'' — the `mf_watch` and `mf_ignore` fields that decide eligibility ([[Watch and ignore fields]], [[Ignore presets]]).
* ''Watcher'' — the part of the daemon that follows filesystem events ([[Watcher]]).
* ''Flush'' — the moment buffered events are applied, after the disk has been quiet ([[Event batching]]).
* ''Reconcile'' — the walk that brings a repository in line with the disk on demand ([[Reconcile]]).
* ''Fingerprint'' — the content hashes by which a moved file is recognised ([[File fingerprint]]).
* ''Candidate'' — a likely move the reconcile will not decide alone ([[Moves and candidates]]).
* ''Orphan'' — a metarecord whose file went away without being asked to ([[Orphans]]).
* ''Mount point'' — a removable volume inside a repository; unplugged, its subtree is ''offline'' ([[Mount points]], [[Offline subtrees]]).
* ''Watch budget'' — the limit on what the inotify watcher may place ([[The watch budget]]).
* ''Broker'' — `metafolder-watchd`, the privileged service watching whole filesystems ([[The fanotify broker]]).

!! History

* ''Event log'' — the history of every write to a repository ([[Event log]]).
* ''Operation'' — one atomic change; ''revision'' — the operations of one request ([[Revisions and operations]]).
* ''HEAD'' — the operation the data currently reflects ([[History tree and HEAD]]).
* ''Rollback'' — moving HEAD elsewhere in the history, files included ([[Rollback]]).
* ''Revert'' — undoing one past revision in place, as a new revision ([[Revert]]).
* ''Undo'' and ''redo'' — taking back the newest change you made, and bringing it back ([[Undo and redo]]).
* ''Pruning'' — dropping old history ([[Pruning the log]], [[Automatic retention]]).

!! Functions

* ''Trash'' — the per-repository bin holding trashed bytes with their metarecords ([[Trash]]).
* ''Duplicate group'' — the metarecord a set of byte-identical files points at ([[Duplicate groups]]).
* ''Tag'' — a metarecord placed in a tree by its path, which other metarecords point at ([[Hierarchical tags]]).
* ''Subsumption'' — having a tag implies having its ancestors ([[Tag subsumption and exclusivity]]).
* ''Link'' — the pairing of a record of one repository with its counterpart in another, which a sync keeps in step ([[Matching records across repositories]]).
* ''Sync plan'' — what a sync will do, written as one metarecord per operation in a repository of its own, before anything happens ([[The sync plan]]).
* ''Snapshot'' — what the two records of a link held at their last sync, in each repository's perspective ([[Change detection in sync]]).

!! GUI

* ''Workspace'' — one tab: a repository and the state of its panels ([[Workspaces]]).
* ''Panel'' — what a slot shows; a ''panel type'' is a kind of panel ([[Panel types]]).
* ''Slot'' — one of the two places a panel is shown in ([[Panel slots and layout]]).
* ''Command'' — a named action, typed, bound to a key or clicked ([[Commands]]).
* ''Command input'' — the line where commands and shell lines are typed ([[The command input]]).
* ''Keybinding'' — a key, or a sequence of keys, running a command ([[Keybindings]]).
* ''Selection'' — the metarecords a panel hands to the others ([[Cross-panel selection]]).
* ''Workspace variable'' — a named value panels of a workspace share ([[Workspace variables]]).
* ''Value picker'' — the completion that fills a reference field ([[Value picker]]).
* ''Shipped script'' — a helper script installed with the configuration, run from the GUI ([[Shipped script]]).
